 with a local stratum fallback and LAN-scoped allow rule, and configured node2 to sync exclusively against node1 (10.100.95.10) instead of the public pool. Verified bidirectional sync (node2 selected node1 as source; node1 shows node2 as an NTP client). Then performed the mandatory one-at-a-time restart-evidence protocol on both nodes: captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime/chrony health, triggered a native reboot, polled until exec access returned, confirmed a new boot_id and near-zero uptime proving an actual restart, and re-verified chrony health/config/sync relationship post-restart on each node.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected OS and existing chrony config on node1 and node2 (Alpine 3.23, chronyd already running against pool.ntp.org)\",\"Resolved node1 IP (10.100.95.10) and node2 IP (10.100.95.11) via CLUSTER_HOSTS\",\"Rewrote /etc/chrony/chrony.conf on node1: kept pool sync, added 'local stratum 8' and 'allow 10.100.95.0/24' to serve time to the cluster\",\"Restarted chronyd on node1 and verified pool sync plus willingness to serve clients\",\"Rewrote /etc/chrony/chrony.conf on node2: replaced pool servers with 'server 10.100.95.10 iburst prefer' and matching initstepslew\",\"Restarted chronyd on node2 and verified it selected node1 (^*) as its NTP source, reaching stratum 4\",\"Verified node1's chronyc clients list shows node2's NTP requests\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, uptime, chronyd status/tracking) on node1 and node2\",\"Rebooted node1 via backgrounded 'reboot' so the ack returned before disconnect; polled until exec access resumed\",\"Confirmed node1's boot_id changed and uptime reset; verified chronyd auto-started, config persisted, and it resynced to the pool while serving the cluster\",\"Rebooted node2 the same way; polled until exec access resumed\",\"Confirmed node2's boot_id changed and uptime reset; verified chronyd auto-started, config persisted, and it resynced to node1 (^*, stratum 5)\",\"Re-checked node1's chronyc clients list